{#
  Shared scripts.

  js/main.js is last on every live page and is the only script all pages share.
  Pages that need more load them BEFORE it — announcements.html loads its data
  file first, members.html loads Leaflet then its data file — because main.js
  reads the DOM those scripts help build. `scriptsBefore` preserves that order.

  main.js is language-aware on its own: it reads document.documentElement.lang
  and picks its four UI strings from an internal dictionary, so there is no
  per-locale script to swap here.
#}
{#- Note: members.html's Leaflet <script> also carries integrity/crossorigin.
    When that page migrates, `scriptsBefore` entries become objects rather than
    bare strings so those attributes survive. Bare strings suffice for now. -#}
{#- A `{locale}` token in any entry is replaced with the locale code, so a page
    can ask for a per-language asset with one line of front matter:
      scriptsBefore: ["/js/announcements-data-{locale}.js"]
    Eleventy renders `permalink` and `eleventyComputed` as templates but NOT
    arbitrary front-matter values, so `{{ locale.code }}` would arrive here
    literally and the page would request a file that does not exist. This is the
    same "state the pattern once, resolve it per locale" idea as `urlPattern`. -#}
{%- for src in scriptsBefore | default([]) %}
<script src="{{ src | replace("{locale}", locale.code) }}"></script>
{%- endfor %}
<script src="/js/main.js"></script>
{%- for src in scriptsAfter | default([]) %}
<script src="{{ src | replace("{locale}", locale.code) }}"></script>
{%- endfor %}
